## Static reasoning

The whole minimal diff, whole new validator, both new regression methods, bootstrap and runtime guard were read. Common and inventory's changed contexts were read and exact inverse byte comparisons establish their otherwise unchanged algorithms. This review does not claim a fresh whole-body review of all 72 legacy tests: their exact bytes were checked against the preserved earlier source reviews.

In `archive_mapping.py:44-55`, the six exceptions require both exact typed raw and designated counterpart tuples. The exception changes only the archive-container clause. Cap, prior-membership, raw/origin identity, release-path, protected four-metadata-path, admission and same-byte conditions remain unconditional. There is no extension-wide `.patch`/`.diff` permission, glob, whitespace waiver, source rewrite, `.gitattributes` change or dropped raw bytes.

In `archive_mapping.py:74-113`, validation still binds checkpoint, parent, actual admission and prior closure, rehashes every role, independently recomputes actual whitespace lines, requires deterministic gzip header bytes, validates the actual standard manifest relation, compares full decoded bytes, and binds the resulting contract to exact logical raw exclusions and tracked gzip/manifest tuples. Common's scope and inventory use the same new archival-text reason literal; their algorithms are unchanged. The prior completed-test empty-fields correction remains unchanged in common.

The positive regression at `tests.py:616-642` checks all six original/counterpart files, uses actual gzip and manifest bytes, invokes the real mapping and SPEC validation, verifies the counted raw/gzip pair and rehashes the inputs afterwards. The negative regression at `tests.py:643-665` covers ten mutations per tuple: aliases, size/hash changes, wrong counterpart, unknown diff, prior membership, releases and protected metadata. Mutated counterparts are deliberately admitted, so wrong-tuple rejection cannot be satisfied solely by a missing-admission error. The release/opaque cases also fail the container clause, so those cases alone do not isolate their dedicated protections; those source guards remain unconditional and unchanged. This is a limitation of those individual negative cases, not an observed bypass.

